# A cell born of an empty literal with no written type cannot say what it
# holds, and the guess annotates the cell with its own symbol (spec § 5,
# design.md §4.5; panel 209's R1). The writes below say nothing more: the
# one mistake is told at the birth, and the cell is poisoned.

function main()
    xs @= []  #~ cannot_infer
    m @= {}  #~ cannot_infer
    xs @ xs.push(1)
    m["a"] @ 1
    print(xs.len() + m.len())
